    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d454">

                <pb facs="0763" n="629" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg629"/>

                <head>No. 454.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pendleton to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-04-02"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 2, 1888</date>.
                        (Received April 16.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 597.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sib</hi>: I inclose herewith clippings and
                    translations from the National Zeitung of the 28th ultimo. They are the only
                    response which I have seen in the Berlin papers to the public telegram touching
                    the message of the President to Congress recommending legislative measures in
                    regard to the exclusion of swine’s meat and the preparations thereof exported
                    from Germany and France.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. H.
                            Pendleton.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d454-a1.xml" xpointer="d454-a1"/>
